These files are real diskutil, bless and nvram outputs recorded on a 14-inch
MacBook Pro (M1 Pro, j314sap) by the Omarchy Mac installer project:

  omacom/omarchy-mac-installer c07e54c2134a8ec1415e7e2b917589ae1d3d7dc9
  Tests/OmarchyAppleInstallerTrustCoreTests/Fixtures/m1-pro-2026-09-28/
    legacy/{list,apfs-list,apfs-volumegroups}.plist, legacy/bless-getboot.txt,
    legacy/info/disk0*.plist,
    legacy/evidence/esp-disk0s4/asahi_stub_info.json (as legacy/asahi_stub_info.json),
    after-make-space/macos-limits.plist, nvram-boot-volume.txt

They are copied unchanged. Sekka's tests read them to build a fake Mac with an
existing Asahi installation on a board the J514S profile doesn't admit.

